<title>CROATIA: SOCCER-GREECE BEAT CROATIA 1-0 IN EURO UNDER-21 QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-GREECE BEAT CROATIA 1-0 IN EURO UNDER-21 QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>KARLOVAC, Croatia 1996-11-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece beat Croatia 1-0</p>
<p>(halftime 0-0) in a European under-21 soccer championship group</p>
<p>one qualifier played on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorer: Nicolaos Lymperopoulos 60</p>
<p>Attendance: 4,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate - played, won, drawn, lost, goals for,</p>
<p>against, points):</p>
<p> Greece	  4  3  0  1  5  3  9</p>
<p> Slovenia	3  2  0  1  4  3  6</p>
<p> Denmark	 2  1  0  1  4  3  3</p>
<p> Bosnia-Herz   3  1  0  2  3  4  3</p>
<p> Croatia	 2  0  0  2  1  4  0</p>
</text>
